          },
          {
            "id": "p31-q9-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P(-4)=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P(1)=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", then solve simultaneously.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx-4$. By the factor theorem, $P(-4)=0$ and $P(1)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(-4)^3+a(-4)^2+b(-4)-4&=0\\\\16a-4b&=68\\\\4a-b&=17\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}1^3+a(1)^2+b(1)-4&=0\\\\a+b&=3\\end{align*}$$\nAdding the two simplified equations:\n$$\\begin{align*}(4a-b)+(a+b)&=17+3\\\\5a&=20\\\\a&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $a+b=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}4+b&=3\\\\b&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
